{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he put upon him the tunic, and girded him with the sash, etc.</b> The order of donning the priestly garments is as follows: tunic, sash, robe, ephod, breastplate, turban, and the golden frontlet — and behold they are seven, which Moses would put on Aaron and place upon him; and together with the breeches, which they would put on themselves first, they are eight. And the order of their donning corresponds to the order of the seven heavens: the breeches, which were to cover the nakedness of the flesh, correspond to the first heaven, in which is the moon, which covers the lower tent of the world — since it too is flesh; the tunic corresponds to the heaven in which is the planet Mercury (כוכב); the sash corresponds to the heaven in which is Venus (נוגה); the robe corresponds to the heaven in which is the sun (חמה); the ephod corresponds to the girding of the heaven in which is Mars (מאדים); the breastplate corresponds to the heaven in which is Jupiter (צדק) — and therefore it was doubled, with the Urim and Thummim, which would give true (מצודקין) utterance in their words; the turban, which is supreme upon the head, corresponds to the heaven in which is Saturn (שבתאי), which is supreme over all the seven — and Scripture called it ״ראש כוכבים״ (chief of the stars); as it is written (Job 22:12): ״וראה ראש כוכבים כי רמו״; the frontlet, upon which is written ״קדש לה׳״, corresponds to the Throne of Glory, which is above the seven. <br>And there is further in the seven garments that Moses would put on him an allusion to the seven known ones (the sefirotic attributes): for the first is the <b>tunic</b> of white linen; the second is the <b>sash</b> with which he would gird him — and strength and might are in the loins; and <b>the robe</b>, which was entirely tekhelet; and <b>the ephod</b>, which was splendor; and <b>the breastplate of judgment</b>, the left leg; and <b>the turban</b>, fitting for a bridegroom; and the seventh, <b>the frontlet</b>, which was of gold — and she is the bride. And understand this."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:04.251437676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}